<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Slovak Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1919 CE · capital Prešov</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Communist puppet state proclaimed in eastern Slovakia in 1919 under the protection of the Hungarian Red Army, which lasted just three weeks.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In May and June 1919 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-red-army">Hungarian Red Army</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hungarian-soviet-republic">Hungarian Soviet Republic</a> pushed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, recently claimed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice">Košice</a> and much of the east. On 16 June 1919, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/presov">Prešov</a>, local and Hungarian communists proclaimed the Slovak Soviet Republic, led by the Czech communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonin-janousek">Antonín Janoušek</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had a Revolutionary Executive Committee modelled on the Hungarian council and copied its nationalisation decrees. It depended entirely on Hungarian troops and found little support among Slovaks, who largely saw it as a Hungarian attempt to reclaim the region.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under Allied pressure, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-red-army">Hungarian Red Army</a> withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> at the end of June 1919, and Czechoslovak forces moved in; the republic collapsed by 7 July 1919. Slovakia remained part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/slovak-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Slovak Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Prešov</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Antonín Janoušek</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Slovak, Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Slovenská republika rád</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=slovak-soviet-republic" aria-label="Slovak Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5170 468 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Slovak Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5490 724L5445 768"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5445 768h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5490 724h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5490 724h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Prešov. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=slovak-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

